<node id="tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001">
  <data key="d0">tb-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-0001</data>
  <data key="d1">table</data>
  <data key="d2">[Table Name]banking_service_financial_limits

This table outlines the financial limits associated with different types of banking services, specifically focusing on cash pickup and cash delivery services offered by the bank. It consists of four columns: 'Type of service', 'Savings (individuals)', 'Senior Citizen / Differently Abled', and 'Current Account Customers'. The table spans two rows of data for both cash pickup and cash delivery services. For both services, individuals can save up to 20,000 per instance, while the limits for Senior Citizens and Differently Abled individuals mirror this amount. However, Current Account Customers have a significantly higher limit of 5 lacs per instance for both services. This creates a noticeable distinction in perceived value and access to banking services across customer categories. Overall, the data reflects the bank's commitment to accessibility for specific groups while still offering considerable limits to standard account holders. The policy with respect to service limits is noted to be subject to change, hinting at flexibility in response to varying bank policies over time.

[Table Footnotes]# Subject to change from time to time as per banks policy.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-574eef8b2a231a2171cb4eadad4c29e5-mm-table-000</data>
  <data key="d4">Door-Step Banking for Senior Citizens and Differently-Abled.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787055132</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
