  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Depositors">
  <data key="d0">Depositors</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Depositors are individuals or entities that place money into a bank, becoming major stakeholders in the banking system and involved in the regulatory framework for banking in India.&lt;SEP&gt;Individuals or entities that deposit money into the bank's accounts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787057501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Financial System">
  <data key="d0">Financial System</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The financial system refers to the broader economic context within which financial institutions operate, including aspects like deregulation of interest rates and banking reforms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-6e9c97657e05cf315dfdf575fb8d6364-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">Deposit Policy.pdf</data>
  <data key="d5">1787057501</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Deposit Products">
  <data key="d0">Deposit Products</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Deposit products are financial products offered by banks to accept deposits from customers, with varied terms and conditions governing their operations.</data>
